  "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
  "body": "That's exactly how it is supposed to work. If you put the images on the queue in fast export mode, you should see the thumbnails decorated with a little \"fast forward ⏩\" icon. But the end result should be nearly indistinguishable from the regular pipeline in most cases (you might in general expect just a small loss of fine detail). The biggest difference is that in fast export mode the image is resized to the bounding box specified in the preferences. I don't remember what happens when the hounds are zero, perhaps fast export is disabled in this case. So maybe the culprit is that you are not able to set the bounds in the preferences window for some reason... But I don't know how that can be. I'll try to investigate ",
